cli-usage = Usage: sim-cli list | run MACHINE [--move a,b | --cycle | --trajectory FILE | --path FILE [--time-optimal]] [--time SECONDS] [--disable-at SECONDS] [--stop-at SECONDS [--stop-category 0|1|2]] [--every STEPS] | analyze MACHINE [--trajectory FILE | --path FILE [--time-optimal]] [--points FILE] [--breakdown FILE] [--budget FILE] | sweep MACHINE [--motor N] [--from HZ] [--to HZ] [--count N] [--amplitude NM] | optimise MACHINE [--runs N] [--nominal] [--pareto FILE] [--path FILE [--time-optimal]] | search MACHINE [--vendor NAME|all] [--series PREFIX] [--gearboxes SERIES] [--axes | --motor-id ID] [--drives paired|neighbours|all] [--rank-by cost|margin|energy|error|thermal|inertia|NAME=WEIGHT,...] [--robust N] [--config FILE --config FILE... [--weights W,W,...]] [--path FILE [--time-optimal]] | transmission MACHINE [--key gearbox.ratio|geometry.pulley_radius_m] [--from V] [--to V] [--count N] [--gearboxes SERIES] | compare-kinematics TASK.toml --machines ID,ID,... [--machine-file FILE]... [--vendor NAME|all] [--series PREFIX] [--gearboxes SERIES] [--drives ...] [--rank-by ...] | verdicts MACHINE [--bands [--samples N [--seed S] | --worst]] [--path FILE [--time-optimal]] | sensitivity MACHINE [--delta FRACTION | --method morris|sobol [--samples N] [--seed S] [--result NAME]...] [--group TABLE]... | step MACHINE [--axis-index N] [--size M] [--time SECONDS] | bode MACHINE [--axis-index N] [--from HZ] [--to HZ] [--count N] [--amplitude M] | tuning MACHINE | margins MACHINE [--bands] | modes MACHINE [--axis-index N] [--points N] [--shapes] | workspace MACHINE [--z Z] [--points N] | replay MACHINE --trace FILE [--map FILE] | fit MACHINE [--trace FILE [--map FILE]] [--sweep FILE [--sweep-motor N] [--amplitude NM]] | fit [MACHINE] --dataset DIR --report DIR | identify [MACHINE] (--trace FILE [--map FILE] [--motor N] [--from HZ --to HZ] [--step-from SECONDS [--step-to SECONDS] [--motor-inertia KGM2]] [--overlay FILE] | --sweep FILE) | check-dataset DIR | compare MACHINE --effect NAME [--signal ID]... [--differences FILE] | stop MACHINE [--category 0|1|2] [--points N] [--path FILE [--time-optimal]] | accuracy MACHINE [--points N] [--repeats N] [--dwell SECONDS] | report MACHINE --out FILE.html | fmu MACHINE --out FILE.fmu [--binary FILE]... [--fmi 2|3]; MACHINE is the id of a registered machine (see list), or left out with --machine-file FILE.toml|FILE.json, a machine defined in a file (not for fmu); for all: [--config FILE] [--catalog DIR] [--motor ARTICLE] [--supply 230v|400v|s120|s210new-230v|s210new-400v|VENDOR-VOLTSv] [--gearbox SIZE-FRAME-RATIO] [--drive ARTICLE] [--belt PROFILE-WIDTH] [--axis NAME] [--set path=value]... [--out FILE] [--lang en|de]. A path file has one piece per line, from where the machine stands: line,a,b (straight to the point), arc,a,b,ca,cb,cw|ccw (on a circle around the centre ca,cb to the point a,b) or spline,a,b (on a smooth curve through the point; lines of spline that follow one another form one curve); on three axes line,x,y,z, spline,x,y,z and arc,x,y,z,cx,cy,cz,cw|ccw (in the plane of start, end and centre). Its timing is planned within the axis limits, with --time-optimal as fast as the motors allow. A file ending in .nc, .ngc, .gcode, .g, .cnc or .tap is read as G-code (G0, G1, G2, G3, F, G17/G18/G19, G20/G21, G90/G91), .src as KUKA KRL (PTP, LIN, CIRC), .mod or .prg as ABB RAPID (MoveL, MoveJ, MoveC), and lines MoveL,MoveJ,MoveC as robot moves (see docs/user-guide.md). Columns and keys named in kg, N, N m, rad or rad/s hold the axis' own unit: on a linear motor N, m/s and m, and the fit report's moved_mass_kg, viscous_friction_n_s_m, coulomb_friction_n and constant_force_n hold kg m2, N m s/rad, N m and N m on a rotary axis. Trailing columns name the units: torque_unit,speed_unit in analyze, speed_unit,torque_unit in --points, torque_unit in --breakdown, search and transmission, units in fit (empty where a row has none). margins leaves crossover_hz and phase_margin_deg empty where the loop has no gain crossover in the band (not measurable; the result is then the gain margin's alone). modes adds mode<i>_small_hz where the machine's small-amplitude modes differ (a gearbox's hysteresis). sensitivity leaves out a value of 0 without a range in [bounds] and names it on the error stream.
cli-error-unknown-machine = Unknown machine: { $arg }
cli-error-bad-argument = Cannot read this argument: { $arg }
cli-error-no-workspace = This machine has no workspace map: it needs three axes and kinematics with a condition number to tell. { $arg }
cli-error-unknown-option = This command has no such option: { $arg }
cli-error-missing-value = This option needs a value: { $arg }
cli-error-conflict = Only one of these options can be given at a time: { $arg }
cli-error-io = File error: { $arg }
cli-error-fmu-binary = The FMU's binary cannot be read; build it with cargo build --release -p sim-fmi, or name it with --binary: { $arg }
cli-search-screened = Not simulated (a part the config cannot take, or a cycle that does not run; the reason is in the table): { $arg } candidates
cli-search-own-gearbox = No gearbox of the series fits, so tried with the config's own gearbox (gearbox empty in the table): { $arg } candidates
cli-search-time = Search time on { $arg }
cli-search-robust-changed = In the error bands (worst corner of each candidate's bounds) the ranking of the best candidates changes: see the columns robust_*
cli-search-robust-same = In the error bands (worst corner of each candidate's bounds) the ranking of the best candidates stays as it is
cli-transmission-optimum = Classic optimum (least torque per unit acceleration) and best value for the cycle of { $arg }
cli-error-worst = --worst needs --bands and goes without --samples and --seed
cli-error-axis-index = --axis-index takes the number of one of the machine's axes, a whole number from 0 to { $arg }
cli-worst-runs = Cycles simulated in the search for the worst corners: { $arg }
cli-optimise-runs = Cycles simulated: search + error bands { $arg }
cli-optimise-runs-worst = Cycles simulated: search + worst corners { $arg }
cli-report-pass = Report written, every check passes: { $arg }
cli-report-fail = Report written, some checks fail: { $arg }
cli-planned-clearance = Planned path: least clearance to the obstacles { $arg } mm
cli-planned-contact = Planned path: first contact with an obstacle at the pose { $arg }
cli-run-clearance = Run: least clearance to the obstacles { $arg } mm
cli-run-contact = Run: first contact with an obstacle (name: time, speed of the tool, pose) { $arg }
cli-run-impact = Run: largest contact force, contact force now and impact energy { $arg }
cli-run-fault = Run: the drives tripped (monitor: motor, time; fault reaction per motor) { $arg }
cli-run-stopping = Run: stopping distance per axis from the trip (the machine stood at) { $arg }
cli-thermal-start-cold = Thermal start: cold (the parts and windings at the temperatures the run began with)
cli-thermal-start-warm = Thermal start: warm, at the rises the cycle settles at; largest change of a rise over the measured pass { $arg } K
cli-thermal-start-unsettled = Thermal start: warm, but NOT converged within the warm passes; largest change of a rise over the measured pass { $arg } K
cli-conveyor = Conveyor: picks, tracking error during the grip along the belt, parts missed { $arg }
cli-stop-worst = Worst stop: triggered at { $arg }
cli-stop-verdict = Stop verdict: { $arg }
cli-accuracy-axis = Accuracy along ISO 230-2, axis { $arg } (B reversal, R bidirectional repeatability, E systematic deviation, M range of the mean deviation, A accuracy)
cli-accuracy-tool = Accuracy at the tool along ISO 9283, over the axes in metres: { $arg } (AP pose accuracy, RP pose repeatability, vAP between the approach directions)
cli-accuracy-verdict = Accuracy verdict: { $arg }

fit-report-written = Report written: { $arg }

cli-sensitivity-zero = Not ranked: { $arg } is 0 and has no range in [bounds] (--delta of 0 is 0); give it one there to vary it.
cli-sensitivity-runs = Cycles simulated for the global sensitivity: { $arg }
cli-measure-first = Measure these first: { $arg }
